<title>CANADA: Queenstake drops on drill results.</title>
<headline>Queenstake drops on drill results.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Queenstake Resources Ltd shares dropped on Thursday on new drilling results from the company's Chupaca mining project in Peru.</p>
<p>Stock in the Vancouver-based company fell C$0.25 to C$1.40 in Toronto after Queenstake said that three new drill holes failed to turn up significant gold deposits.</p>
<p>&quot;People are impatient for success. They were expecting us to have spectacular results and hit on the first hole,&quot; said Doris Meyer, Queenstake vice president of finance.</p>
<p>The company is prospecting in Peru on more than 60,000 hectares of land bordering Barrick Gold Corp's  prized Arequipa mining project.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416-941-8100</p>
</text>
